window.docContents[132].resolve({"/Tier-2___-definitions/Symbolic___Specifications___/Symbolic.Specifications.Concrete.ExternInterpretation/#file-Symbolic___Specifications___Concrete___ExternInterpretation":{"contents":"Paper › Symbolic/Specifications/Concrete › ExternInterpretation.leanTier 2 · definitions\n\nTier 2 · definitions used by the symbolic proof 4 headline theorems depend on it 81 of 135 lines trusted trust banner B2, trusted: definitions used by the statement source ↗Read the definitions shown. Only the declarations that the headline statements use are shown, with the namespace, section, open and variable commands needed to read them. The collapsed runs are theorems, which Lean checks, and definitions that no headline statement uses.\n\nDeclarations on this page (10)abbrev ByteStringabbrev ExternInterpretationdef x25519TorsionSymboldef torsionShiftdef shaStateBytesdef shaStateOfBytesdef sha256CompressFunctionstructure ExternCryptoLawsHolddef X25519TorsionFreedef X25519TorsionShiftsRejected\n\nCryptographic Extern Interpretations and LawsTrusted: definitions used by the statement.Byte-level interpretation of external cryptographic primitives called by the signal-session binary, together with the algebraic and torsion-check laws assumed by the refinement and security statements.\n\n\n\nabbrev ByteStringL31 ↗#\n\nabbrev ExternInterpretationL33–34 ↗#Partial byte-level semantics symbol → args → Option ByteString for external functions.\n\n\n\ndef x25519TorsionSymbolL43–44 ↗#Spec-only symbol adding the t-th Curve25519 8-torsion point to a 32-byte u-coordinate.\n\ndef torsionShiftL46–53 ↗#Adds the t-th 8-torsion point to point via x25519TorsionSymbol, returning point when t = 0, point is not 32 bytes, or the result is not 32 bytes.\n\ndef shaStateBytesL55–58 ↗#Encodes a SHA-256 chaining state as eight little-endian 32-bit words.\n\ndef shaStateOfBytesL60–64 ↗#Decodes eight little-endian 32-bit words from bytes (zero-filling missing bytes).\n\ndef sha256CompressFunctionL66–69 ↗#Lifts sha256CompressSymbol to a compression function on ShaState.\n\nstructure ExternCryptoLawsHoldL71–106 ↗#Algebraic and output-length laws assumed of X25519, AES-256-CBC with strict PKCS#7 padding, and HMAC-SHA256.\n\n\n\ndef X25519TorsionFreeL114–119 ↗#Whether PublicKey::is_torsion_free accepts the 32-byte Montgomery key b after decompressing it to an Edwards point.\n\ndef X25519TorsionShiftsRejectedL121–136 ↗#Requires X25519TorsionFree to reject any 32-byte key whose u-coordinate equals a non-trivial 8-torsion shift of an X25519 public key.\n\n\n\n","context":"AlphaProof Code: Verifying Signal’s Security at the Machine-Code Level","header":"Symbolic/Specifications/Concrete/ExternInterpretation.lean","id":"/Tier-2___-definitions/Symbolic___Specifications___/Symbolic.Specifications.Concrete.ExternInterpretation/#file-Symbolic___Specifications___Concrete___ExternInterpretation"}});